# variants/base/portage/package.use/14-rust — Rust: the toolchain. Images ship rust-bin; dev-lang/rust
# is catalog-only (kits/core/portage, `#dev-lang/rust`): these flags are how the binhost builds it.
#
# Numeric prefix: Portage reads this directory in sorted order and the LAST
# file wins a conflict (measured 2026-09-13), so the number is precedence, not
# decoration. Ranges: 00-09 hardware · 10-19 languages and toolchain ·
# 20-39 system and graphics · 40-49 applications · 50-69 axis and flavor
# layers · 90-99 late overrides.

# Flags removed 2026-09-09: absent from the package's IUSE, so Portage was
# ignoring them in silence. Verified token-by-token against the ebuilds and the
# md5-cache of both repos. Removed here: dev-lang/rust[profiler]; dev-lang/php[xmlrpc]; dev-java/openjdk[gentoo-vm].

# Rust
# No llvm_slot pin here any more: the global LLVM_SLOT is 22 and every current
# dev-lang/rust declares LLVM_COMPAT=( 22 ), so the default already fits.
dev-lang/rust clippy llvm_targets_WebAssembly lto rustfmt rust-analyzer rust-src rust_sysroots_wasm system-llvm
dev-lang/rust-bin clippy rustfmt
